 in a file with `--db PATH`. One lock guards all access, and the hit counter is incremented in SQL, so concurrent redirects are counted correctly.\n- **Codes:** 6 random characters from `A-Za-z0-9`, regenerated on the rare collision. The same URL always gets the same code.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_shortener.py` covers the following.\n  - Creating and deduplicating links.\n  - The 400 cases.\n  - Redirects and hit counts.\n  - 404s.\n  - A non-ASCII URL.\n  - Links and hit counts surviving a restart with `--db`.\n- **README:** `README.md` has usage, the API summary and how to run the tests.\n\n**Choices the spec didn't dictate**\n- URLs containing whitespace or control characters, and URLs with an invalid port, get a 400. This stops a bad URL from injecting extra headers into the `Location` response.\n- In the `Location` header, non-ASCII characters are percent-encoded, because HTTP headers can't carry them raw. The `url` in JSON responses is the original string.\n- Request bodies over 64 KB and URLs over 8192 characters get a 400.\n\nThe suite takes about 4 seconds. I didn't look into why.","ttft_ms":7536,"type":"result","duration_ms":50981,"uuid":"3ac41a90-0e24-44d6-bfb8-e539741764b8","ttft_stream_ms":3089,"time_to_request_ms":1846,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":455,"system_prompt":194,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":8,"input_attachments":113,"input_hooks":17,"tool_pool_refresh":3,"init_message":10,"engine_pickup":14,"autocompact":1,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":955,"message_normalization":13,"client_creation":8,"request_build":53},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":1642,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":192,"time_to_request_major_faults":94,"first_content_frame_ms":3100,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
